name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-lesson5-level8_2025'
title 'Conditional Logic'

wrong 'Change the condition to `batteryPercent === 20`.'
wrong 'Change `batteryPercent` to `19` so it prints the right message.'
wrong 'Swap the two messages inside the `if` and `else` blocks.'
right 'Change the condition to `batteryPercent <= 20` .'
allow_multiple_attempts false

markdown <<MARKDOWN
**Scenario**: Battery Saver should turn ON at 20% or below.

Given code:
```
let batteryPercent = 20;
let msg;

if (batteryPercent < 20) {
  msg = "Battery Saver ON";
} else {
  msg = "Normal Mode";
}

console.log(msg); // Output: Normal Mode
```

The output at 20% is `Normal Mode,` but the requirement says it should be `Battery Saver ON`.

**Which change is the best fix so the rule works for all battery levels?**

MARKDOWN

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN

A. triggers only at exactly 20%, not “20% or below.”

B. only “fixes” the example value (20 → 19) but fails for other levels (e.g., 20, 18, 21).

C. breaks low-battery behavior: at 5% it would say “Normal Mode,” which is wrong.

D. fixes the boundary: “20% or below” → <= 20. Works for 0–20 (Saver ON) and 21+ (Normal).
MARKDOWN
